    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Summary\n\nI'm trying to use agent-orchestrator with a local directory using git without a remote repo. Adding the local directory, I'm getting an error message. \n\nIs there any way around this or is it a bug or is it a feature? \nHow can I make it work without actually using a remote repo? \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a project in directory `/home/michael/projectname`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCreate a project in directory `/home/michael/projectname`\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nWon't create a project in directory `/home/michael/projectname`\n\n`\nProject added, but orchestrator did not start: spawn projectname-1: workspace:\nworkspace: default branch is unresolved: repository\n\"/home/michael/projectname\" has no remote or AO-recorded\ndefault; configure this repository's primary remote and cached HEAD (for\nexample, git -C \"/home/michael/projectname\" remote set-head\n<remote> <branch>) and retry (DEFAULT_BRANCH_UNRESOLVED)\n` \n\n### AO version\n\nv0.12.9\n\n### Environment\n\nLinux lenovo 6.8.0-136-generic #136~22.04.1-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri Jul  3 16:29:11 UTC  x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux\n\n### Logs / extra context\n\n```shell\n\n```\n\n### Before submitting\n\n- [x] I searched existing issues for duplicates\n- [x] I removed secrets / tokens from logs and screenshots",
